<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eastern States Agency</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eastern States Agency was a political agency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> formed in 1933 to supervise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chota-nagpur-plateau">Chota Nagpur</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, about forty states in all. It took over the work of the Orissa and Chhattisgarh state superintendents. After independence its states were merged into Orissa, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> in 1948.</p></div>
